# Angles. A degree is `45°`, and degrees, minutes and seconds of arc are
# written together, `45°30′30″` (`º`, `'` and `"` do for `°`, `′` and `″`).
# The radian `rad` is the unit of an angle, a steradian `sr` is a radian
# squared, and a lumen `lm` and a lux `lx` need it. An angle is a dimension of
# its own, so a frequency in `Hz` and a speed of turning in `rad.s^-1` are not
# mixed up.
#
# `sin`, `cos` and `tan` take an angle in any unit and work in radians; `dms`
# writes an angle out as degrees, minutes and seconds.

sheet Literals

| Name          | Value             |
| ------------- | ----------------- |
| degrees       | 45°               |
| minutes       | 45°30′            |
| seconds       | 45°30′30″         |
| ascii         | 45º30'30"         |
| decimal       | 45°30.5′          |
| radians       | = pi() / 2 * 1rad |
| angular speed | 2rad.s^-1         |
| solid angle   | 2sr               |
| luminous flux | 800lm             |
| illuminance   | 500lx             |
| celsius       | 20°C              |

sheet Arithmetic

| Name             | Value                     |
| ---------------- | ------------------------- |
| sum              | = 45° + 0.5rad            |
| difference       | = 90° - 30°30′            |
| in radians       | = 180°.to('rad')          |
| in seconds       | = 1°.to('″')              |
| equal            | = 45°30′ == 45.5°         |
| sine             | = sin(30°)                |
| cosine           | = cos(60°)                |
| tangent          | = tan(45°)                |
| uncertain sine   | = sin(30.0(5)°)           |
| written out      | = 45.508333333°.dms(1)    |
| a radian         | = dms(1rad)               |
| illuminance      | = (800lm / 2m^2).to('lx') |
| Euler's identity | =e()**(1i*pi())           |

# Trigonometry in degrees and radians, with `pi()` for the radians. A `Float`
# is not exactly equal to anything it is nearly (`cos(90º)` is 6e-17, not 0),
# so `==` is false where `=~=`, which allows a difference of 1e-15 of the
# larger side, is true. Converting to radians and back comes home too.
sheet Trigonometry


| Name                           | Value                                 |
| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------- |
| sine of 30º                    | = sin(30º)                            |
| same in radians                | = sin(pi() / 6 * 1rad)                |
| they agree                     | = sin(30º) =~= sin(pi() / 6 * 1rad)   |
| sine of 30º is a half          | = sin(30º) =~= 0.5                    |
| cosine of 60º                  | = cos(60º) =~= cos(pi() / 3 * 1rad)   |
| tangent of 45º                 | = tan(45º) =~= tan(pi() / 4 * 1rad)   |
| cos of a right angle           | = cos(90º)                            |
| cos of a right angle (rounded) | =cos(90º).round(-16)                  |
| is it zero                     | = cos(90º) == 0                       |
| is it nearly zero              | = cos(90º) =~= 0                      |
| sin of a half turn             | = sin(pi() * 1rad) =~= sin(180º)      |
| half turn                      | = 180º =~= pi() * 1rad                |
| full turn                      | = 360º =~= 2 * pi() * 1rad            |
| a turn is not half             | = 180º =~= 2 * pi() * 1rad            |
| round trip                     | = 90º.to('rad').to('º') =~= 90º       |
| round trip, written            | = (pi() / 2 * 1rad).to('º')           |
| back from seconds              | = 1°.to('″').to('°') =~= 1°           |
| sin² + cos²                    | = sin(40º) ** 2 + cos(40º) ** 2 =~= 1 |

# A column of angles is shown in the unit it names, `Angle[°]`, whatever the
# cells were written in, and a bare number is read in it.
sheet Bearings

Place    : String
Bearing  : Angle[°]
Radians  : Angle[rad; .3f]
Written  : String
Quadrant : Angle[rad; .3f]

| Place   | Bearing       | Radians | Written | Fraction | Quadrant | Check |
| ------- | ------------- | ------- | ------- | -------- | -------- | ----- |
| ,       | 0°            | *       | *       | 0/1      | *        | *     |
| east    | 90°           | *       | *       | 1/4      | *        | *     |
| south   | = pi() * 1rad | *       | *       | 1/2      | *        | *     |
| lookout | 120°30′       | *       | *       | 1/3      | *        | *     |
| summit  | 45.5          | *       | *       | 1/4      | *        | *     |

Radians := Bearing.to('rad')
Written := Bearing.dms()
Quadrant := 2*pi()*1rad*Fraction
Check := Bearing==Quadrant
